{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-8","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：不可公度量与可公度量与比例","englishTitle":"If two magnitudes have not to one another the ratio which a number has to a number, the magnitudes will be incommensurable.","book":10,"number":8,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.8","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.8/","group":"prop_1","sourceNumber":8,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-8@raw-b83e5864102d8597","contentId":"euclid-10-8","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"b83e5864102d8597b9216110b7f63c69b49abd782b0583fa9837f5a12fc58aed","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-8.statement","euclid-10-8.construction.1","euclid-10-8.proof.1","euclid-10-8.proof.2","euclid-10-8.conclusion","euclid-10-8.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-8.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-8","revisionId":"euclid-10-8@raw-b83e5864102d8597","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"4e410a21639847f5ae6edb742354e257d62657d38f4e4f20c12c74e9e07a7179","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If two magnitudes have not to one another the ratio which a number has to a number, the magnitudes will be incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果两个星等之间没有对应的数值比,则该星等为不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-8.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-10-8","revisionId":"euclid-10-8@raw-b83e5864102d8597","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8c4190d84766be1bc9567dc2e38f4aa298dd4b03e08555455307641b6a3b651f","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let the two magnitudes A, B not have to one another the ratio which a number has to a number; I say that the magnitudes A, B are incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因为,两个星等A,B, 不必彼此对应一个数值与一个数值的比;我说,A, B是不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-8.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-8","revisionId":"euclid-10-8@raw-b83e5864102d8597","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"e9d4ac468256225036fcb20a9b41dc35e4c75b395fb27f459ef2d4cfafd7a96c","citations":["euclid-10-5"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if they are commensurable, A will have to B the ratio which a number has to a number. [[X. 5](/principles/euclid-10-5)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果是可公度,A将达到B,而数字则等于数字。 [[X. 5](/principles/euclid-10-5)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-8.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-8","revisionId":"euclid-10-8@raw-b83e5864102d8597","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0a4198c4a3c5da998bedc6076e16f163465aaa0fef49049b1e50c0ab857d7f21","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it has not; therefore the magnitudes A, B are incommensurable."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但并没有,因此,A,B是不可公度。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-8.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-8","revisionId":"euclid-10-8@raw-b83e5864102d8597","order":4,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"6d0def46992eb0b105b82d6bce6477450c524a884c436026a0e1ed896becf6c9","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由此命题得证。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-8.source","contentId":"euclid-10-8","revisionId":"euclid-10-8@raw-b83e5864102d8597","order":5,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"df9926f65e2cf4fba2cc0701417ac2c52b5ef1fdde1f216337b33cb265264b66","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.8/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.8\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-8:euclid-10-5:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-8","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-8.proof.1"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-5","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.8","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.8/","sourceLabel":"X. 5"}}],"incomingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-11:euclid-10-8:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-11","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-11.proof.5"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-8","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.11","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.11/","sourceLabel":"X. 8"}}],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-10-8:euclid-10-5:explicit","id":"euclid-10-5",